Name:P17 - a "safe" block with the best creature into open pump mana (round 1029 study F1, Insane I1 T13; round 1035)
Description:The opponent attacks with Watchwolf (3/3) and two Leonin Skyhunters (2/2 flying). The AI, at 14 life, has Bladewing the Risen (4/4 flying, its 6-drop) and Dragonmaster Outcast (1/1) untapped. The opponent has Forest and Plains untapped and Giant Growth plus two cards in hand. Bladewing blocking anything is "safe" on the board (it kills a 3/3 or a 2/2 and survives) and dies to Giant Growth. Stock Forge blocks the Watchwolf with Bladewing and loses it. With TRICK_ALLOWANCE_ON_BLOCK (Default.ai) Bladewing is no safe block: it is worth more than either attacker and dies to the attacker at +3/+3 (green open). The AI takes 7 (14 -> 7): with the pump counted on an unblocked attacker that leaves 4, not in danger by Default.ai's AI_IN_DANGER_THRESHOLD. (The study's own position was 11 life: 7 on the board plus a +3 pump leaves 1, so the AI is in danger and still trade-blocks with Bladewing, as stock does.) Expect: Bladewing survives the turn. Guard: P17b (no open mana, no hand: the block is right).
Turns:1
